<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'"><title>Tavi · A little world</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="./world/style.css"></head>
<body><main>
<header><a class="brand" href="./index.html"><img src="./icon.svg" width="28" height="28" alt="">TAVI <span>/ COMPANIONS</span></a><nav><button id="return-to-tavi" hidden disabled type="button" class="host-return">← Back to Tavi</button><a href="./cat-study.html">Character studio</a><span class="version">World prototype · 0.6.10</span></nav></header>
<section class="introduction"><div><p class="eyebrow">A HOME. A PERSONALITY. A LITTLE MAGIC.</p><h1>A world of their own.</h1><p>Stay a while. See where curiosity leads.</p></div><button id="portrait-button" class="portrait-button" aria-label="Choose your companion"><canvas id="portrait" width="360" height="360" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span id="portrait-hint">? Choose a companion</span></button></section>
<section class="world-shell" aria-label="Continuous companion home">
<div class="world-top"><span class="live"><span></span>ONE CONTINUOUS HOME</span><span id="art-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading painted characters…</span><div class="camera-tools"><button id="pan-left" aria-label="Pan camera left">←</button><button id="follow" aria-pressed="true">Follow companion</button><button id="pan-right" aria-label="Pan camera right">→</button></div></div>
<div class="viewport" id="viewport"><canvas id="world" tabindex="0" aria-label="Side-scrolling home. Drag to look around, or use the camera buttons. Use the object buttons below to invite your companion."></canvas><div class="welcome" id="welcome"><p class="eyebrow">SOMEONE NEW IS WAITING</p><h2>Every little life starts somewhere.</h2><button id="choose" class="primary">Choose your companion</button></div></div>
<div class="world-bottom"><span id="where">Kitchen · Dining room</span><label class="pan-label">Look around<input id="pan" type="range" min="0" max="1400" value="200" aria-label="Camera position across the home"></label><span class="hint">Drag the scene to explore</span></div>
</section>
<div class="below-world"><section class="company"><p class="eyebrow" id="emotion">A LITTLE LIFE, AT ITS OWN PACE</p><h2 id="companion-name">Your companion</h2><p id="thought" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose the ? portrait to meet a companion.</p><div class="invites"><button data-object="snack">Offer a snack <small>Kitchen</small></button><button data-object="table">Come sit with me <small>Dining room</small></button><button data-object="honey">Share some honey <small id="honey-remaining">10 servings left</small></button><button data-object="bath">Prepare a bath <small>Bathroom</small></button><button data-object="bed">Suggest a nap <small>Bedroom</small></button><button data-object="toy">Bring out the ball <small>Garden</small></button></div><div class="small-actions"><button id="refill-honey">Refill honey jar</button><button id="pet">Pet</button><button id="look">Look at me</button><button id="wave">Ask for a wave</button><button id="pause" aria-pressed="false">Pause world</button></div><p class="help">Objects have their own effects and availability. The honey jar holds ten servings and can be refilled. Your companion may decide what to visit.</p><details><summary>Little memories <span class="muted">· this visit</span></summary><ul id="memories"><li>A new home, with room for new habits.</li></ul></details></section>
<aside><section class="details-card"><p class="eyebrow">PAINTED COMPANIONS</p><h2>Their own little world.</h2>
<label class="field" for="name">Name <span class="muted">· optional, chosen by you</span></label>
<input id="name" maxlength="32" placeholder="Their name is yours to choose">
<label class="field" for="form">Companion</label><select id="form"><option value="cat">Cat</option><option value="unicorn">Unicorn</option></select>
<p class="help">Only the hand-painted Cat and Unicorn have complete character art right now. View their motions and color palettes in the <a href="./cat-study.html">character studio</a>.</p>
<label class="care-toggle"><input id="care" type="checkbox"> Try gentle care <span>Optional needs; no offline decay in this prototype.</span></label><div id="needs" class="needs" hidden></div><details id="traits" hidden><summary>Individual traits <span class="muted">· evolve through experience</span></summary><ul id="trait-list" aria-label="Companion traits"></ul><p id="trait-evolution" role="status" class="help" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="help">Original Tavi adaptive genes evolve in response to completed activities and bonding, with diminishing influence and no offline evolution. Painted Cat or Unicorn appearance remains your choice.</p></details></section></aside></div>
<footer><p>Development preview · standalone sessions stay local to this visit; Tavi host saves the companion privately when supported</p><p>Camera behavior is provisional. Individual traits gradually evolve with experiences; no breeding system is required. Growth stages, multiplayer and wallet integrations remain future work. <a href="./credits.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Art & credits</a></p></footer>
<dialog id="selection"><button id="close-selection" class="close" aria-label="Close companion selection">×</button>
<p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE YOUR PAINTED COMPANION</p><h2>Who will share your little world?</h2>
<p>Only characters with a complete painted rig are available.</p><div id="forms" class="forms">
<button data-form="cat"><canvas width="360" height="320" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Cat<small>Painted fur · expressive ears · curling tail</small></button>
<button data-form="unicorn"><canvas width="360" height="320" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>Unicorn<small>Painted coat · flowing mane · gentle horn</small></button></div>
<p class="help">The older procedurally drawn creatures and pixel-art collection have been retired, not substituted for these painted animals.</p></dialog>
</main><script src="./chunks/000.js"></script><script src="./chunks/001.js"></script><script src="./chunks/002.js"></script><script src="./chunks/003.js"></script><script src="./chunks/004.js"></script><script src="./chunks/005.js"></script><script src="./chunks/006.js"></script><script src="./chunks/007.js"></script><script src="./chunks/008.js"></script><script src="./world-main.js"></script></body></html>
